column in \code{aes()} or a fixed value in \code{geom_cob()}.
\item \code{unpollinated} gives the percentage of unpollinated kernels, from 0 to 100. These
kernels are removed starting from the tip, with an irregular edge. The cob keeps its
full length: if \code{x} is yield, the bare tip is part of the bar.
